<earl:TestResult rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/swo_prov#Report_r1_themis_test_114">
  <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Entity"/>
  <earl:outcome rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/ns/earl#failed"/>
  <prov:wasGeneratedBy rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/swo_prov#Check_r1_themis_test_114"/>
  <prov:value>Themis tests: 29/35 CQs pass all their tests. FAILING TESTS:
CQ05:
  modification domain Tool -&gt; Absent
CQ11:
  Software SubClassOf ComputationalArtifact -&gt; Absent
CQ32:
  helpMechanism domain HelpResource -&gt; Absent
  helpMechanism range HelpResource -&gt; Absent
CQ46:
  Entity developmentActivity string -&gt; Conflict
CQ54:
  version domain Software -&gt; Absent
CQ59:
  Permissiveness permissivenessLevel string -&gt; Conflict
Fix each failing test in the ontology: Undefined = add the term under exactly that name; Incorrect = declare it with the right type; Absent = add the tested axiom so the knowledge is modelled; Conflict = the ontology contradicts the test, correct the axioms.</prov:value>
</earl:TestResult>

